+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `.feature` specs and referenced `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Voyage 1 scope
+
+TodoMVC app, vanilla JS, localStorage persistence. Eight feature files, 26 scenarios, 130 steps. All steps undefined; QM dispatches Crew to build verification support and production code together.
+
+Key assets: `assets/app-spec.md` (product spec), `assets/app-template.index.html` (base markup). CSS from `todomvc-app-css` and `todomvc-common` already in RIGGING.md dependencies.
+
+localStorage key convention: `todos-vanillajs`.
diff --git a/features/adding-todos.feature b/features/adding-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..66a9aa2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/adding-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+Feature: Adding todos
+  As a user
+  I want to add new todo items
+  So that I can track tasks I need to complete
+
+  Rule: New todo creation
+
+    Scenario: Adding a todo by pressing Enter
+      Given the app is open
+      When the user types "Buy milk" in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+      And the new-todo input is empty
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: Empty input is not created as a todo
+      Given the app is open
+      When the user types "   " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then no todos exist in the todo list
+      And the main section is hidden
+
+    Scenario: Input is trimmed before creating a todo
+      Given the app is open
+      When the user types "  Buy milk  " in the new-todo input and presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
diff --git a/features/completing-todos.feature b/features/completing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c077fd7
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/completing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Completing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to mark todos as completed
+  So that I can track what I have finished
+
+  Rule: Individual todo completion
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the toggle checkbox marks a todo as completed
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle for "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the class "completed"
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+    Scenario: Unchecking a completed todo makes it active again
+      Given the app is open
+      And a completed todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the toggle for "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not have the class "completed"
+      And the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+  Rule: Mark all as complete
+
+    Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox marks all todos as completed
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      Then all todos have the class "completed"
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+      And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+    Scenario: The toggle-all checkbox unchecks when a single todo is unchecked
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+      And the user clicks the toggle for "Buy milk"
+      Then the toggle-all checkbox is unchecked
diff --git a/features/deleting-todos.feature b/features/deleting-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..92fa26f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/deleting-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+Feature: Deleting todos
+  As a user
+  I want to remove todos I no longer need
+  So that my list stays clean
+
+  Rule: Destroy a todo
+
+    Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes the todo
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user clicks the destroy button for "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+      And the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: Clear completed
+
+    Scenario: The clear completed button removes all completed todos
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+      And the todo "Walk dog" appears in the todo list
+      And the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+    Scenario: The clear completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the clear-completed button is hidden
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..cddba9e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user
+  I want to edit the title of a todo
+  So that I can correct or update my tasks
+
+  Rule: Editing a todo
+
+    Scenario: Double-clicking a todo enters editing mode
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the class "editing"
+      And the edit input for "Buy milk" is focused
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Enter while editing saves the new title
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then a todo "Buy oat milk" appears in the todo list
+      And the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Blurring the edit input saves the new title
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Escape
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+
+    Scenario: Pressing Escape discards changes
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user types "Buy oat milk" in the edit input
+      And the user presses Escape
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+      And the todo "Buy oat milk" does not exist
+
+    Scenario: Editing to empty destroys the todo
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the user double-clicks the todo "Buy milk"
+      And the user clears the edit input
+      And the user presses Enter
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not exist
diff --git a/features/footer.feature b/features/footer.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..c3918a2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/footer.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Feature: Footer and counter
+  As a user
+  I want to see how many active todos I have
+  So that I know my remaining workload
+
+  Rule: Counter display
+
+    Scenario: The counter shows the number of active todos
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk", "Walk dog", and "Read book" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      Then the todo count shows "2 items left"
+
+    Scenario: The counter uses singular form for one active todo
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the todo count shows "1 item left"
+
+    Scenario: The counter uses plural form for zero active todos
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      And the todo "Walk dog" is completed
+      Then the todo count shows "0 items left"
+
+  Rule: New input autofocused
+
+    Scenario: The new-todo input is focused when the page loads
+      Given the app is open
+      Then the new-todo input is focused
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..bd4ec47
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose my work
+
+  Rule: Todos persist to localStorage
+
+    Scenario: Todos survive a page reload
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then a todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+
+    Scenario: Completed state persists across reload
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the page is reloaded
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" has the class "completed"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..7aa732e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Routing
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todos by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed work
+
+  Rule: Default route
+
+    Scenario: All todos are shown by default
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" appears in the todo list
+      And the "All" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Active filter
+
+    Scenario: Only active todos are shown on the active filter
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/active"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" does not appear in the todo list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" appears in the todo list
+      And the "Active" filter is selected
+
+  Rule: Completed filter
+
+    Scenario: Only completed todos are shown on the completed filter
+      Given the app is open
+      And todos "Buy milk" and "Walk dog" exist
+      And the todo "Buy milk" is completed
+      When the user navigates to "#/completed"
+      Then the todo "Buy milk" appears in the todo list
+      And the todo "Walk dog" does not appear in the todo list
+      And the "Completed" filter is selected
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..35c8910
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+Feature: Visibility based on todo count
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show and hide sections based on whether I have todos
+  So that I see only relevant UI
+
+  Rule: No todos present
+
+    Scenario: The main section and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+      Given the app is open
+      Then the main section is hidden
+      And the footer is hidden
+
+  Rule: Todos present
+
+    Scenario: The main section and footer are shown when there are todos
+      Given the app is open
+      And a todo "Buy milk" exists
+      Then the main section is visible
+      And the footer is visible
